WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.087
Child processes may inherit environment variables from the parent Python
process unless the application controls the environment explicitly.

2
00:00:08.087 --> 00:00:20.054
That inherited state can include API keys, tokens, passwords, connection
strings, private key paths, proxy settings, debug flags, cloud
configuration, feature flags, executable search paths, and library paths.

3
00:00:20.054 --> 00:00:25.182
Even when the child program is trusted, it rarely needs everything the
parent process knows.

4
00:00:25.182 --> 00:00:29.522
A safer pattern is to construct an explicit environment for the approved
task.

5
00:00:29.522 --> 00:00:36.491
Pass only the variables needed for that operation, and avoid letting
untrusted input change behavior-affecting variables.

6
00:00:36.491 --> 00:00:46.222
This makes subprocess behavior more predictable and reduces blast radius
if the child process fails, logs its environment, spawns another tool, or
writes diagnostic output.

7
00:00:46.222 --> 00:00:50.102
Environment minimization is both a security control and a review aid.

8
00:00:50.102 --> 00:00:55.427
Secrets should not be placed in command arguments unless there is a
carefully justified reason.

9
00:00:55.427 --> 00:01:05.421
Depending on the operating system and tooling, arguments may appear in
process listings, monitoring systems, job metadata, crash output, logs,
diagnostics, or support bundles.

10
00:01:05.421 --> 00:01:08.840
Standard input can also be risky when it is captured or logged.

11
00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:15.481
The stable principle is to provide the least sensitive material necessary
through the narrowest appropriate channel.

12
00:01:15.481 --> 00:01:19.229
Inherited user permissions matter as much as inherited variables.

13
00:01:19.229 --> 00:01:24.620
A subprocess normally runs with the parent process identity or a
configured execution identity.

14
00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:30.538
If that identity has broad filesystem, network, or secret-store access,
the child process may have it too.

15
00:01:30.538 --> 00:01:39.480
Secure subprocess usage treats identity, permissions, environment, and
configuration as part of the command contract instead of invisible
background state.
